      "text": "---\n\n# 🚀 **MOCHA + CHAI NOTES **\n\n---\n\n# 🟩 **MOCHA — Test Runner**\n\nMocha is a **JavaScript test framework** that helps you **run tests**, structure them, and handle async operations.\n\n### ✅ **Key Features**\n\n* Runs tests in **describe()** and **it()** blocks\n* Supports **async testing** (callbacks, promises, async/await)\n* Works with **Node.js**, and can also be used in frontend tests\n* Flexible — you choose your own assertion library (Chai)\n\n---\n\n# 📌 **Mocha Syntax**\n\n### **Basic Structure**\n\n```js\nconst assert = require('assert');\n\ndescribe(\"Math Tests\", () => {\n  it(\"should add numbers correctly\", () => {\n    let result = 2 + 3;\n    assert.equal(result, 5);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### **Async Test Example**\n\n```js\nit(\"should fetch user async\", async () => {\n  const user = await getUser();\n  assert.equal(user.name, \"John\");\n});\n```\n\n### **Before / After Hooks**\n\n```js\nbefore(() => console.log(\"Run once before all tests\"));\nbeforeEach(() => console.log(\"Before each test\"));\nafter(() => console.log(\"After all tests\"));\nafterEach(() => console.log(\"After each test\"));\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔥 **When using Mocha in MERN**\n\nYou’ll use Mocha to test:\n\n* API routes\n* Controllers\n* Database (MongoDB) logic\n* Utility/helper functions\n\n---\n\n# 🟥 **CHAI — Assertion Library**\n\nChai is used with Mocha to **write human-readable test assertions**.\n\nThree assertion styles:\n\n1. **Assert** (classic)\n2. **Expect** (popular, readable)\n3. **Should** (BDD style)\n\n---\n\n# 📌 **Chai Setup**\n\n```js\nconst chai = require(\"chai\");\nconst expect = chai.expect;\n```\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "---\n\n# 🚀 **MOCHA + CHAI NOTES **\n\n---\n\n# 🟩 **MOCHA — Test Runner**\n\nMocha is a **JavaScript test framework** that helps you **run tests**, structure them, and handle async operations.\n\n### ✅ **Key Features**\n\n* Runs tests in **describe()** and **it()** blocks\n* Supports **async testing** (callbacks, promises, async/await)\n* Works with **Node.js**, and can also be used in frontend tests\n* Flexible — you choose your own assertion library (Chai)\n\n---\n\n# 📌 **Mocha Syntax**\n\n### **Basic Structure**\n\n```js\nconst assert = require('assert');\n\ndescribe(\"Math Tests\", () => {\n  it(\"should add numbers correctly\", () => {\n    let result = 2 + 3;\n    assert.equal(result, 5);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### **Async Test Example**\n\n```js\nit(\"should fetch user async\", async () => {\n  const user = await getUser();\n  assert.equal(user.name, \"John\");\n});\n```\n\n### **Before / After Hooks**\n\n```js\nbefore(() => console.log(\"Run once before all tests\"));\nbeforeEach(() => console.log(\"Before each test\"));\nafter(() => console.log(\"After all tests\"));\nafterEach(() => console.log(\"After each test\"));\n```\n\n---\n\n# 🔥 **When using Mocha in MERN**\n\nYou’ll use Mocha to test:\n\n* API routes\n* Controllers\n* Database (MongoDB) logic\n* Utility/helper functions\n\n---\n\n# 🟥 **CHAI — Assertion Library**\n\nChai is used with Mocha to **write human-readable test assertions**.\n\nThree assertion styles:\n\n1. **Assert** (classic)\n2. **Expect** (popular, readable)\n3. **Should** (BDD style)\n\n---\n\n# 📌 **Chai Setup**\n\n```js\nconst chai = require(\"chai\");\nconst expect = chai.expect;\n```\n\n",
